## Workspace Setup (Monorepo)

### pnpm Workspaces

```yaml
# pnpm-workspace.yaml
packages:
  - "apps/*"
  - "packages/*"
```

```json
// Root package.json
{
  "name": "monorepo",
  "private": true,
  "scripts": {
    "build": "pnpm -r build",
    "test": "pnpm -r test",
    "lint": "pnpm -r lint"
  }
}
```

### Shared Dependencies

```json
// packages/shared/package.json
{
  "name": "@company/shared",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "main": "./dist/index.js",
  "types": "./dist/index.d.ts",
  "exports": {
    ".": {
      "import": "./dist/index.js",
      "types": "./dist/index.d.ts"
    }
  }
}
```

## .npmrc Configuration

```ini
# .npmrc
engine-strict=true
save-exact=true
auto-install-peers=true

# For private registries
@company:registry=https://npm.company.com/
//npm.company.com/:_authToken=${NPM_TOKEN}
```

## Conventions

- Use pnpm for new projects (faster, stricter)
- Pin Node.js version with `engines` field
- ALWAYS commit lock files
- Use `type: "module"` for ES modules
- Run security audits in CI
- Keep dependencies up to date (weekly review)
- Document any third-party dependencies with licensing implications
- NEVER use deprecated or unmaintained packages

## Anti-Patterns

- ❌ Not committing lock files
- ❌ Using `*` or `latest` for versions
- ❌ Ignoring security vulnerabilities
- ❌ Installing unnecessary dependencies
- ❌ Mixing package managers in one project
- ❌ Using `npm install` without `--save` or `--save-dev`
- ❌ Installing dev dependencies in production
- ❌ Not specifying Node.js engine version

**See also:** `security.mdc`, `testing.mdc`
